WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.580
Sometimes, too much of a good thing is a bad
thing.

00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:07.860
Such is the case for Gemini Man, director
Ang Lee's action thriller featuring not one

00:00:07.870 --> 00:00:13.700
but two Will Smiths, one an aging assassin
named Henry Brogan, played by Smith in a live-action

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:17.200
performance, and another nicknamed "Junior,"
a young clone of Henry sent to kill him, which

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:18.980
Smith portrayed through motion-capture.

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:24.100
"Ten years from now there will be court cases
where people are like, 'I swear to God, that's

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:25.020
not me.'"

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:30.520
With Academy Award winning director Lee at
the helm, action movie icon Jerry Bruckheimer

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:34.399
set as producer, Smith in the leading role,
and David Benioff, one half of the Game of

00:00:34.399 --> 00:00:38.109
Thrones showrunning team, with a credit on
the screenplay, Gemini Man seemed to have

00:00:38.109 --> 00:00:40.680
everything going for it, on paper, at least.

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:45.320
But after literal decades of development,
the movie sadly opened in theaters to a decidedly

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:46.519
muted response.

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:47.880
"'Cause I'm the best."

00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:51.080
"You are obviously not the best."

00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:56.020
In its opening weekend that officially began
on Friday, October 11, Gemini Man earned a

00:00:56.031 --> 00:00:58.659
measly $20.5 million domestically.

00:00:58.659 --> 00:01:03.879
Internationally, the film pulled in $39 million,
bringing its worldwide debut total to just

00:01:03.880 --> 00:01:10.580
$59.5 million, several million dollars under
its reported production budget of $138 million.

00:01:10.580 --> 00:01:16.060
To put things into perspective, $59.5 million
is about what Fast &amp; Furious spinoff Hobbs

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:19.380
&amp; Shaw yielded during its opening weekend
in North America alone.

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:23.799
It's also a little more than what John Wick:
Chapter 3 earned in its first few days out,

00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:25.120
also just domestically.

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:28.020
So, why did Gemini Man bomb at the box office?

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:29.180
Let's take a look.

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:34.080
Gemini Man had the unfortunate fate of opening
the same weekend as a family-friendly animated

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:38.000
movie, which tends to draw in a good chunk
of change regardless of its quality, and the

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:42.760
weekend after one of the most talked-about
films of fall 2019 made its bombastic debut.

00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:46.960
Though the majority of critics weren't impressed
by it, MGM's The Addams Family managed to

00:01:46.969 --> 00:01:51.920
take in $30.3 million domestically thanks
to its star-studded voice cast, including

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:55.380
Charlize Theron as Morticia and Oscar Isaac
as Gomez.

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:59.939
Released in time for Halloween, The Addams
Family attracted audiences of all ages, sliding

00:01:59.939 --> 00:02:04.579
into second place at the weekend box office,
absolutely crushing Gemini Man but not even

00:02:04.580 --> 00:02:07.220
coming close to toppling the film in first
place.

00:02:07.220 --> 00:02:11.700
It should come as no surprise that the number-one
movie of the weekend was Joker, Todd Phillips'

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:14.740
gritty character study of the infamous DC
Comics villain.

00:02:14.740 --> 00:02:18.920
Starring Joaquin Phoenix as Arthur Fleck,
a failed comedian who experiences something

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:23.950
of a psychotic break and transforms into the
Joker, the film earned another $55 million

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:30.040
domestically and $125.7 million internationally
in its second weekend at the box office, bringing

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:34.940
its total to-date box office take-home to
$543.9 million.

00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:39.860
It's also a bona fide cultural sensation,
and basically all anyone can talk about lately.

00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:44.200
So it's not shocking that Gemini Man got bested
by the Clown Prince of Crime.

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:48.700
It's not really Gemini Man's fault that it
was up against some fierce competition, but

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:52.300
unfortunately, critical reception to the film
has also been less-than-optimal.

00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:56.720
On Rotten Tomatoes, Gemini Man holds a 25
percent approval rating from critics, who

00:02:56.730 --> 00:03:01.400
have taken issue with the movie's frustrating
story, its uninspired script, and visual effects

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:03.320
that only sometimes impress.

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:08.240
One critic hated Gemini Man so much that he
described it as, quote, "an absolutely inexcusable

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:09.060
turkey."

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:13.540
Had Gemini Man been a critical success, it
may have had a better chance at the box office.

00:03:13.820 --> 00:03:18.920
Though Gemini Man tanked hard in its opening
weekend, it still has a tiny chance at success.

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:22.540
The Hollywood Reporter has noted that the
film is set to make a splash in China, where

00:03:22.549 --> 00:03:24.819
it will launch on Friday, October 18.

00:03:24.819 --> 00:03:28.579
However, unless the film pulls in hundreds
of millions of dollars in that international

00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:32.660
market, Gemini Man could end up costing its
financial backers a ton of money.

00:03:32.660 --> 00:03:36.939
Sources for Deadline have indicated that studio
Paramount Pictures is looking at a loss of

00:03:36.940 --> 00:03:39.400
about $60 million on Gemini Man.

00:03:39.520 --> 00:03:41.120
"Henry, has this ever happened to you before?

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:42.900
Your own government trying to kill you?"

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:45.380
"Nah, that's new."

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:49.620
The bright side of this is that Gemini Man's
scant box office earnings probably won't get

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:51.000
director Ang Lee down.

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:54.900
He shared with Forbes that he doesn't believe
financial performance is the definitive marker

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:56.060
of a film's worth.

00:03:56.060 --> 00:04:00.069
Lee also shared that he still stands by his
past films, despite some of them performing

00:04:00.069 --> 00:04:01.400
poorly at the box office.

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:02.460
Lee explained,

00:04:02.460 --> 00:04:07.019
"You don't judge something by its financial
success or not...I can argue this all day.

00:04:07.020 --> 00:04:08.020
I've been there before.

00:04:08.020 --> 00:04:12.200
My last movie, Billy Lynn, I felt that I was
right, and the whole world was wrong, but

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:13.220
it doesn't matter."

00:04:13.220 --> 00:04:16.660
Some may agree with Lee, and others may think
he's talking crazy.

00:04:16.660 --> 00:04:20.750
Either way, Gemini Man underperformed in its
first weekend out, and it's looking like that

00:04:20.750 --> 00:04:22.880
might spell big trouble moving ahead.

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:24.500
"I don't want to shoot you!"

00:04:24.620 --> 00:04:26.180
"Mind if I shoot you?"

